{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdfYJd4aVLBLY1j2fLX25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## CLDW Gender Balance\n\nCounting across all **80 texts** in the corpus:\n\n| Gender | Texts | Share |\n|--------|-------|-------|\n| Male (M)   | **74** | 92.5% |\n| Female (F) | **6**  | 7.5%  |\n\nThe 6 female-authored texts come from just **5 unique women** (Harriet Martineau contributes two):\n\n- **Celia Fiennes** — *Through England on a Side-Saddle* (1698)\n- **Ann Radcliffe** — *A Journey Made in the Summer of 1794* (1795)\n- **Priscilla Wakefield** — *A Family Tour through the British Empire* (1804)\n- **Catherine Hutton** — *Oakwood Hall* (1819)\n- **Harriet Martineau** — *A Complete Guide to the English Lakes* (1855) and *The Lights of the English Lakes* (1861)\n\nBy **unique author** (72 authors total, deduplicating repeat contributors), the split is **67 male / 5 female** — the same ~93% / 7% imbalance.\n\n**Assessment:** The corpus is heavily male-dominated, with women accounting for only about 1 in 13 texts (and 1 in 14 authors). This reflects the historical realities of who published Lake District writing between 1622 and 1900, but it means the CLDW is far from gender-balanced."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56683,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56683},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb0ef0bd-e999-48ff-9094-633a6795d5b8","uuid":"65d675aa-3f02-4c70-9d6f-9568a07a5a6f","request_id":"req_011CdfYJbr9fM2YJosABM2HP"}
